        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ciIsz",
          "name": "Section Shot view — /set/[label]/shot/[key]",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 14,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "AAnf7",
              "name": "st",
              "fill": "$ink",
              "content": "Shot view — /set/[label]/shot/[key]",
              "fontFamily": "$font-display",
              "fontSize": 24,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "nc2Fy",
              "name": "note",
              "fill": "$ink-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1000,
              "content": "One screenshot from a set, read in depth beside a design board. Pressing a screenshot in the set viewer opens it here as a modal, with the set kept mounted beneath it so its filters and scroll survive a close; the same address loaded on its own renders expanded, as a page, with the way back to the set in place of the close button. There is no before side and no bucket: a set screenshot is not a comparison. The board pane, the zoom bars and the box toggle are the comparison modal's design view, unchanged. Below both panes, the spacing readings list every reading the capture measured — design token, raw value on the scale, off-scale, exempt — not only what changed, so the simplest story reads in full: Badge — Accent is 8px of --space-2 either side and a 2px pill half-step top and bottom. Token and exempt are the neutral tone; only raw-on-scale and off-scale take warning. A set captured without a token ledger, which today is every baselines screenshot, opens the same view and says so in two sentences: the screenshot and the board are still worth reading. The title is the way out to the story itself: viewport/theme · set is underlined and opens the dev Storybook (localhost:6006), drawn as a link only while the console runs in development and as plain text otherwise; the arrow-out square opens the published Storybook in the shot's theme — acceptance-gate only, since no child publishes one.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
